{"source": {"title": "浣溪沙·一曲新词酒一杯", "author": "晏殊", "text": "一曲新词酒一杯，去年天气旧亭台。夕阳西下几时回？
无可奈何花落去，似曾相识燕归来。小园香径独徘徊。"}, "translation": "A new tune, a cup of wine,
Last year's weather, the same old terrace;
The sun sinks west—when shall it return?

Helplessly the blossoms fall and go,
Familiar swallows come back, as of old;
Alone I linger on the scented path of the small garden."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "**Butterflies Love Flowers: I Lean on the High Tower**

I linger, leaning on the high tower, in the gentle breeze;
My gaze stretches to the far horizon where spring sorrow grows,
Dim and heavy, rising from the edge of the sky.

Amidst the green grass and misty light of the setting sun,
Silent, who understands my meaning as I lean on the railing?

I intend to act with unbridled wildness, seeking drunken bliss;
To raise a glass, to sing aloud—forced joy tastes bitter still.

My robe bands loosen day by day, yet I regret nothing at all;
For her sake, I willingly waste away through weariness and decline."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "**Butterfly in Love with Flower**
*By Liu Yong*

I linger, leaning against the high tower, as the breeze blows gently;
Extending my gaze to the far horizon, spring’s sorrow rises darkly from the sky.
Amidst the grassy hues and misty light of the fading sun,
In silence, who can understand the meaning behind my reliance on the railing?

I intend to cast aside restraint, seeking oblivion in drunkenness;
Facing wine and singing songs, I force myself to joy, yet it turns tasteless.
Though my belt grows loose bit by bit, I shall never repent;
For her sake, I willingly endure this withering away."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I lean long on the tower, the wind a whisper thin;
I gaze to the far edge—spring sorrow, dim,
Rises from the rim of the world.

Grass fades in mist and the last of the light;
No one can read my silence, my railing-bound plight.

I vow to drink wild, to seek one drunken night,
To sing before the cup—yet forced joy is no delight.
My belt grows loose, yet I would not repent;
For her, I gladly wear myself away."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I lean upon the high tower, a slender wind caressing;
Gazing far, the spring's sorrow rises dimly from the sky.
In fading light, grass and mist glow softly, dying—
Silent, who could know the heart behind this railing?

I resolve to be wild, to seek one deep and drugged oblivion;
Wine raised, song sung—yet forced joy turns to nothingness.
My belt grows loose, my frame grows thin, yet never shall I grieve;
For her I would wither to the bone, and count it sweet."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I lean long on the high tower, the breeze thin and fine;
gazing far, spring sorrow rises dim from the edge of the sky.
Grass-green, mist-light, in the fading glow of sunset—
silent, who understands the meaning of my leaning on the railing?
I meant to be reckless, seek one drunken night;
wine before me, song upon my lips—forced joy still tastes of nothing.
My belt grows loose, yet I repent not;
for her I waste away to hollow cheeks."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I lean against the high railing, the fine wind blowing;
Looking far into spring sorrow, darkening at the horizon’s edge.
In the fading light, grass and misty haze blend together;
Silent, who understands my meaning as I rely on the rail?

I plan to be unrestrained, seeking a drunken stupor;
To sing with wine in hand, but forced joy has no taste.
My robe grows loose, yet I regret nothing in the end;
For her sake, it is worth wasting away until I am haggard."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I lean upon the high tower, standing long;
A gentle breeze blows faint and soft.
My gaze extends to the horizon’s end, where sorrow blooms,
And dimly rises from the distant sky.

Grass hues blend with misty light beneath the setting sun;
In silent longing, who can know my heart’s true intent?

I plan to live freely, seeking drunkenness for solace,
Singing loud while drinking deep—yet forced joy tastes of ash.

Though my belt grows loose day by day, I never regret this fate;
For her sake, I allow myself to waste away."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "To the Tune of "Butterflies Love Flowers"

I lean upon the high tower, where the breeze blows soft and fine;
Gazing far into spring’s sorrow, dark melancholy rises from the skyline.
Grass hues in misty light, bathed in the fading sunset glow;
Silent, who can comprehend my meaning as I rest against the railing?

I plan to seek wild abandon, aiming for a single drunkard’s trance;
Facing wine, singing aloud, yet forced joy tastes of emptiness.
My belt grows looser day by day, yet I regret nothing at all;
For her sake, I endure this wasting, pale and worn away."}

{"source": {"title": "蝶恋花·伫倚危楼风细细", "author": "柳永", "text": "伫倚危楼风细细，望极春愁，黯黯生天际。
草色烟光残照里，无言谁会凭阑意。
拟把疏狂图一醉，对酒当歌，强乐还无味。
衣带渐宽终不悔，为伊消得人憔悴。"}, "translation": "I stand long, leaning on the high tower, the breeze thin;
gazing far, spring sorrow rises dim at the sky's edge.
In the setting glow, grass-green and misty light—
silent, who can read the heart behind the rail?

I plan a wild recklessness to drink myself drunk;
wine before me, song to sing—
forced merriment still tastes of nothing.
My belt loosens day by day, yet I never regret;
for her I waste away to pallor, and to lean."}

{"source": {"title": "静夜思", "author": "李白", "text": "床前明月光，疑是地上霜。
举头望明月，低头思故乡。"}, "translation": "Before my bed, the bright moonlight gleams;
I wonder if it's frost upon the ground.
I raise my head to gaze at the bright moon,
Then bow down low and think of home so fond."}

{"source": {"title": "鹿柴", "author": "王维", "text": "空山不见人，但闻人语响。
返景入深林，复照青苔上。"}, "translation": "Empty mountains, no one in sight;
Yet voices echo through the height.
Last light returns to deep forest glades,
And falls once more on mossy shades."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "A morning rain has settled Wei's light dust;
The travelers' inn is green, the willows newly bright.
Come, friend, drain one more cup of wine before you go—
West of Yang Pass, no old friend meets your sight."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "Morning rain at Weicheng dampens the light dust;
The inn's willows are fresh and green.
I urge you to drink one more cup of wine—
West of Yang Pass, there will be no old friends."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "At Dawn in Wei City Before You Leave for Anxi

The morning rain has wet the dust in Wei;
Fresh green willows shade the inn where we stay.
I beg you, drink this cup of wine once more—
West of Yang Pass, no old friend awaits you there."}

{"source": {"title": "鹿柴", "author": "王维", "text": "空山不见人，但闻人语响。
返景入深林，复照青苔上。"}, "translation": "Deer Enclosure

Empty mountain, no one in sight;
Yet human voices echo and ring.
The setting sun’s light pierces the deep woods,
And once again falls upon the green moss."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "At Weicheng, morning rain dampens the light dust;
The inn is green, the willows fresh and new.
I urge you, friend, to drink one more cup of wine—
West of Yang Pass, no old friend will you find."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "Morning rain at Wei City moistens the light dust;
Green willows by the inn gleam, vividly new.
Drain one more cup of wine, I beseech you—
West of Yang Pass, no old friend remains."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "In Wei City, morning rain has settled the light dust;
The inn is green, its willows bright with new life.
I urge you to drain one more cup of wine,
For west of Yang Pass, there are no old friends left."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "The morning rain of Wei Town has dampened the light dust;
the inn's green willows shine in a fresh, vivid hue.
I urge you to drain one more cup of wine—
west of Yang Pass, you will meet no old friend."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "At Yellow Crane Tower, an old friend bids westward farewell;
In the mist and blossoms of March, he journeys east to Yangzhou.
His lone sail’s distant shadow fades into the boundless blue sky;
Only the River flows on, meeting the horizon’s edge."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "Farewell, old friend, west of the Yellow Crane Tower—
amid the flower-mist of the third month, he drifts down to Yangzhou.
The lone sail's far shadow ends at the rim of blue sky;
all that is left is the Long River, flowing to the horizon."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My old friend bids Yellow Crane Tower farewell,
and sails east to Yangzhou through March's misty blossoms.
A lone sail—its far shadow lost in the boundless blue;
I see only the Long River flowing to the sky's rim."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My friend, west of the Yellow Crane Tower, takes his leave;
Amid flowers and mist in March, he sails down to Yangzhou.
A lone sail's far shadow dissolves into the endless blue—
I see but the Yangtze, flowing to the rim of the sky."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My friend bids farewell to the Yellow Crane Tower in the west,
In the misty flowers of March, he sails down to Yangzhou.
His solitary sail, a distant shadow, fades into the blue sky’s end;
Only the Yangtze River is seen flowing toward the edge of heaven."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My old friend bids farewell to Yellow Crane Tower in the west,
Amid mist-blossoms of the third month, he sails down to Yangzhou.
A solitary sail, a distant shadow, vanishes into the boundless blue sky;
Only the Yangtze River flowing to the edge of the heavens is seen."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My old friend bids farewell at West Yellow Crane Tower,
Amid mist and blossoms of March, he sails down to Yangzhou.
His solitary sail, a distant shadow, vanishes into the blue sky’s end;
I see only the Yangtze River flowing toward the horizon’s edge."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "**Spring View**

The nation shattered, yet the mountains, rivers stand;
Spring fills the city, grass and trees grow deep.
Grieving the times, the flowers splash with tears;
Loathing parting, birds alarm the heart.
Beacon fires have blazed three months unceasing;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
White-haired, I scratch—and the strands grow shorter still,
So sparse they can no longer hold a hairpin."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "Spring Prospect

The realm lies shattered, yet the hills and streams endure;
Spring visits the city—grass and trees grow thick, untamed.
Touched by these times, the flowers weep;
Grieved by parting, birds' cries wound the heart.
For three months the beacon fires have burned;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
I scratch my white hair thinner still—
Now too sparse to hold a single pin."}

{"source": {"title": "黄鹤楼送孟浩然之广陵", "author": "李白", "text": "故人西辞黄鹤楼，烟花三月下扬州。
孤帆远影碧空尽，唯见长江天际流。"}, "translation": "My old friend bids farewell at Yellow Crane Tower, westward bound no more;
In the third month of blossoming mist he sails downstream to Yangzhou.
A lone sail, its shadow grows faint, swallowed by the boundless blue sky—
All I see is the Yangtze river flowing to the edge of the world."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "**Spring Prospect**

The realm lies shattered—mountains and rivers remain;
Spring fills the city, grass and trees grow deep.
Moved by the times, flowers bring tears;
Grieving farewell, birds startle the heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three months;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
My white hair, scratched ever shorter,
Barely holds a hairpin now."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "The Nation Falls

The state is shattered, yet mountains and rivers remain;
In the city’s spring, grass and trees grow thick and wild.
Moved by the times, flowers bring tears to my eyes;
Grieving at parting, birds’ songs startle my heart.
Beacon fires have blazed for three months on end;
A letter from home is worth gold in its ten thousand weight.
I scratch my white hair, finding it ever thinner—
So sparse that soon I’ll be unable to hold even a pin."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "The nation broken, mountains and rivers remain;
Spring in the city, grass and trees grow deep.
Touched by the times, flowers splash with tears;
Hating parting, birds startle the heart.
Beacon-fires have burned three months on end—
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
I scratch my white hair, ever thinner;
Hardly enough left to hold a hairpin."}

{"source": {"title": "春望", "author": "杜甫", "text": "国破山河在，城春草木深。
感时花溅泪，恨别鸟惊心。
烽火连三月，家书抵万金。
白头搔更短，浑欲不胜簪。"}, "translation": "**Gazing at Spring**

The nation broken, yet mountains and rivers remain;
Spring returns to the city—grass and trees grow deep.
Grieved by these times, flowers draw out tears;
Hating farewell, birds' cries pierce the heart.
Beacon-fires have raged three months without cease;
