{"source": {"title": "登高", "author": "杜甫", "text": "风急天高猿啸哀，渚清沙白鸟飞回。
无边落木萧萧下，不尽长江滚滚来。
万里悲秋常作客，百年多病独登台。
艰难苦恨繁霜鬓，潦倒新停浊酒杯。"}, "translation": "Fierce the wind, high the sky, gibbon cries in grief;
Clear the islets, white the sand, birds wheeling back.
Boundless leaves rustle down;
Endless river rolls on.
Ten thousand miles, grieving autumn, ever a stranger;
A lifetime, racked by illness, alone I mount the height.
Hardship and bitter grief have frosted my thickening hair;
In ruin, newly I set down my cup of turbid wine."}

